    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Amid milder spring weather, a seasonal rise in movement brought hope for stability even as people seeking a better life were apprehended at the southwest border. Observers noted the increase in apprehensions, from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March, while policies designed to create order kept immigration statistics near multi-decade lows, reflecting an enforcement policy outcome sought by many. Leaders trying to find a way forward remained deadlocked in a legislative stalemate over separate funding, an unresolved challenge that left the path to repair unclear.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
