    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows, an enforcement policy outcome shaped by restrictive measures in place along the U.S. border. This low crossing numbers trend persisted even as favorable conditions contributed to a statistical trend: apprehensions rose from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. Witnesses to the situation saw hope for stability remains, yet the legislative impasse in Congress left those caught in a difficult system awaiting resolution, a failure to find common ground that tests public trust.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "why-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "center": "result-0",
