      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.62
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Legislators faced a political deadlock over funding for immigration enforcement agencies in a pending reconciliation package, a failure to find common ground that deepened the legislative impasse. Security analysts and policy observers watched as spring weather drew people affected by policy toward the border area, leading to a numerical change in apprehensions. Yet the border security effect of existing enforcement policy outcome kept crossings low, offering a fragile hope that sincerity and repair might yet guide leaders toward resolution.",
